WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.336
-John, welcome back to the show.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:06.840
I gotta say, you were
our first in-person guest

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.708
when we didn't have an audience,

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.910
and now we have a full audience,
so thank you for coming back.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.412
-Jimmy, the last time
we saw --

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.114
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.782
This is -- This is amazing.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:18.050
I mean,
last time we were together,

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.351
we were wearing body condoms.

00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:20.786
I think there were
ten people here.

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:22.989
-That's correct.
We were like 20 feet apart.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.758
-They tested me in the lobby,
and I don't ever want to --

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:28.361
-We don't talk about that.
Yeah. Of course. Yeah. I --

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:30.095
-Good to have you back.
This is --

00:00:30.095 --> 00:00:31.464
-Doesn't it feel good?

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.466
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.835
-I love a live audience.
I really do.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.203
-You miss it, right?
-I do.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.472
-You live for it. But, I mean,
that's why we love you.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.740
But I remember you said to me,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.509
"Jimmy, I got to be
the first guest.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:44.243
If you're going
back to the studio,

00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:45.644
I want to be the first guest."

00:00:45.644 --> 00:00:47.646
And I was like, "Great,
but we don't have an audience."

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:49.481
You go, "I'm just gonna
do it just because --

00:00:49.481 --> 00:00:51.383
Just for 'The Tonight Show'
and just for you."

00:00:51.383 --> 00:00:52.685
And I appreciate that.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.654
-Man, I love you.
-I know. I love you right back.

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:57.290
-Well -- Okay. So wait a second.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.792
Usually,
if I were to be vulnerable,

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:01.860
you would make fun of me.
-Yeah.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.896
-And that's kind of
how our relationship goes.

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:06.032
I say I love you,
and you say, like --

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:09.035
-Yeah, make fun of you.
But COVID's changed me.

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:10.536
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.838
Now I accept the love,
and I give the love back.

00:01:12.838 --> 00:01:14.573
-It must be you guys.
Thank you so much!

00:01:14.573 --> 00:01:16.475
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you so much.

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.611
-No, I'm about to -- No, no.
I'm about to make fun.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.313
Now I'm about to --
Now I can make fun.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.915
I do -- I do --
I do just appreciate you.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:24.783
And I -- But I want
to get into some stuff.

00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:26.686
"Vacation Friends," congrats on,
by the way.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:27.853
-We got to talk about that.

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:29.155
-We have to talk
about "Vacation Friends."

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.389
-Or else the bosses
will kill me.

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:31.924
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
But I want to talk about --

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:34.527
We got -- Football is back.
-Football is back!

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.761
-It's happening right now.

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:38.565
So, we got
the Bucs versus Dallas.

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.966
I know you're a New England boy.

00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:43.236
-Yeah, I was born
in New England.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.705
-Yeah, and so
you're a Patriots fan,

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.240
or a Tom Brady fan at one point.
-I am a Tom Brady fan.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.743
And just like Tom Brady,
I have moved to Tampa Bay.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.846
-You actually did.
-I was there first.

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.546
I have this secret --
Really, honestly.

00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:57.016
I have this secret theory
that Tom Brady is stalking me.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:02:00.019
-Yeah. He's following you.
-We're both 44.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.621
I grew up in New England.
He moved to New England.

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:03.923
-That's close enough.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.891
-We've both won
respective championships

00:02:05.891 --> 00:02:07.993
in our respective fields.

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:11.631
I moved to Tampa.
He followed me to Tampa.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.799
-I'm just saying.

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:16.002
Have you guys ever hung out?
Have you ever crossed paths?

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.803
-No, but I see these
weird security cameras

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.672
that have been stationed
around my property,

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.140
and I think
maybe he's behind it.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.309
-Yeah, he's behind that.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:27.180
This summer, you came back
to WWE for SummerSlam,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.315
and it was honestly so exciting.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.717
-Dude, it was great!
I had a wonderful match.

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:34.153
I finished second place.
-No, that's not the way --

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:37.156
No, no. That's not
the way wrestling works.

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:38.491
I'm sorry.
-Says you!

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.092
-That's not the way
wrestling works.

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:41.694
Roman Reigns.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.263
It was awesome, by the way,
just to see you back there.

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:45.898
Because we talked,
and I was like,

00:02:45.898 --> 00:02:47.734
"There's hints of you
maybe coming back."

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.668
And you're like, "I don't know."
Because you have --

00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:51.437
You had "Suicide Squad."

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.372
You got the -- You had
the show that's happening,

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:54.774
the series
that's coming out now.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:57.309
And you go, "I'm not sure."
Then what happened? WWE --

00:02:57.309 --> 00:02:59.245
-I had a month off,
and they were like,

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.980
"Hey, you want to come to work?"
And I was like, "Do I?!"

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.381
And they said that
live audiences were back,

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:04.483
and I love live audiences!

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:06.619
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.588
-But how did it feel --
how did it feel

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:12.525
to get back in the ring,
get the jorts back on?

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.260
-Well, I mean, that was nice.
-Yeah.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.928
-That was nice.
-You looked great.

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:19.131
-There is no better feeling
than being in front

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:20.799
of a live audience.
There really isn't.

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:22.568
And I'm so grateful
to have all of you here.

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:24.437
I'm so grateful to be back
with a live audience.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:27.906
There is no other energy
like performing and entertaining

00:03:27.906 --> 00:03:29.776
or telling stories
or just shooting the [bleep]

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:31.343
in front of a live audience.

00:03:31.343 --> 00:03:33.079
-So thank you very much.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.981
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.583
-You remember --
Do you remember the first time

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.885
you actually wrestled
in front of an audience?

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:41.654
-Yes, I do.
-Where was this?

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.724
-It was in a gym called
L.A. Boxing in Orange County,

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:47.527
and seven people were there.

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:50.563
And I was not good.
So nothing's really changed.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:51.664
-No. Yeah, right.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.032
But did you feel it?
Were you nervous?

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.600
What -- Did you come out
and you were like --

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.068
-Oh, man.
I'm nervous behind the curtain.

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:57.503
Like, I'm always nervous.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.038
I think
if you lose those nerves,

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.074
if you lose that anticipatory
excitement, like,

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.975
"Oh, I don't know
how this is going to go,"

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:04.343
like, you got to move on.

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:05.845
I think you're done
at that point.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.647
I think you should
always have that energy.

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:09.348
-Because I know
you do love what you do.

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:10.783
-Yeah, this is fun.
-I know.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.718
-We're just talking,
and people are listening.

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:13.953
This is great.

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:16.789
Or you're not listening.
You're texting. Whatever.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.358
-The people at home, yeah.
-They're not listening, either.

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:20.860
-When you were --

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.129
-"Why is he interviewing no one?
Why is it just an empty chair?"

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:25.531
-They don't see you here.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.700
But this is before
you were John Cena,

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.636
before you were a WWE superstar.

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:33.972
You were known as...
"The Prototype."

00:04:33.972 --> 00:04:36.876
-I was.
Can you -- That's a --

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:38.310
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.312
-You were jacked.
-That's a crazy picture.

00:04:40.312 --> 00:04:42.348
So, that was taken
pre-cellphone camera.

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:44.517
And that was a candid
by one of my friends.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.984
I had to cover up my man bits

00:04:45.984 --> 00:04:47.987
'cause I was going
to the bathroom.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.688
-That is not true at all.
-That is not true at all.

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:53.792
-No, but explain to me
the name "The Prototype."

00:04:53.792 --> 00:04:57.930
-So I was 50% man, 50% machine,

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.732
and 100% awful.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.701
It was bad. It was --
-It was a bad --

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:05.304
-It was bad.
-Well, I have video of you

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:08.141
trash-talking
and promoting as The Prototype.

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:09.841
-No way!
-And you guys, judge.

00:05:09.841 --> 00:05:11.944
See if you remember this.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.080
-I look
in your genetic lunch box

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.715
and find a peanut-butter
and jelly sandwich

00:05:16.715 --> 00:05:18.617
with the crusts cut off!

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:22.321
I am 50% man...

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:24.389
50% machine!

00:05:24.389 --> 00:05:27.960
You are 100% fatality!

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.662
[ Growls ]

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.197
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:32.698
-A peanut-butter
and jelly sandwich!

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:35.134
-With the crusts cut off!
Come on!

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:38.637
-Come on, man!
-Come on.

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:40.939
-What do you remember?

00:05:40.939 --> 00:05:43.009
-That -- So, that was done --
We were --

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.444
There was a documentary crew
following us around.

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:47.513
And we usually have --
And this is done in --

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.115
That was in Southern California.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.384
But when you learn your craft,

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:54.120
part of that
is impromptu promo class

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.388
where they just put
a bunch of people in a room,

00:05:56.388 --> 00:05:58.124
and the job is to try
to catch you off guard.

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.559
And everybody
was kind of stumbling,

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:01.694
and they just asked me to get
up there and say something,

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.562
so I came up with that
on the spot

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:05.297
and threw it out there,
and they actually put it on TV.

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:09.535
So that actually -- that
"genetic lunch box" monologue

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.370
kind of kicked
the whole thing off for me.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.239
So I wouldn't be anywhere
if it wasn't for a peanut-butter

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:14.740
and jelly sandwich
with the crust cut off.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.242
-There you go. You're right.
Now -- Yeah.

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:17.543
-Weird story.

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.645
-Look at you now, though.
"Vacation Friends."

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:21.079
This is the biggest original --

00:06:21.079 --> 00:06:23.182
Hulu original film
in Hulu history.

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:25.084
-People actually watched
and actually laughed.

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:26.852
-It's really funny.
-And I'm so grateful.

00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:29.154
Thank you all for watching.
Thank you guys for watching.

00:06:29.154 --> 00:06:31.123
-It's so good.
"Vacation Friends."

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:33.226
They're making a sequel.
Already signed up for a sequel.

00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:34.894
-Number two.
There's number two on the way.

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:37.163
Which is kind of the story
of everybody's lives.

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:39.531
-There's number two on the way.
-There's number two on the way.

00:06:39.531 --> 00:06:41.067
Just waiting
for that next number two.

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.701
-You have great chemistry
with Meredith.

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:44.370
You had great chemistry.
Lil Rel, we know.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.905
-Lil Rel's the best.
-He's been on the show.

00:06:46.905 --> 00:06:48.974
you know what I was
going to say to Lil Rel?

00:06:48.974 --> 00:06:51.209
Because when I've seen him
do stand-up --

00:06:51.209 --> 00:06:53.679
I saw him at this charity
he did for Dennis Leary

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:56.048
called "Comics Come Home"
in Boston.

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:59.018
And he was so funny,
but his laugh makes me laugh.

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:00.385
He's got like a,
"Yeh-yeh-yeh."

00:07:00.385 --> 00:07:02.454
Or something like a weird --
He's got a weird laugh,

00:07:02.454 --> 00:07:04.089
and he didn't use it
in this movie.

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:06.425
And I'm like -- That's
the secret move that he has.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:09.061
-Saving it for the sequel.
Spoiler alert!

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:10.495
-It is so funny, though.

00:07:10.495 --> 00:07:13.232
If I can set the stage --
Let me do my job a little bit.

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:15.234
So, basically,
what happens is...

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:16.502
Lil Rel and his fiancée --

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:18.237
or, at the time,
his girlfriend --

00:07:18.237 --> 00:07:20.640
go on vacation, and he's
about to propose to her.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.407
And their room is destroyed

00:07:22.407 --> 00:07:25.077
because the person
who's staying upstairs

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:26.912
destroyed it,
overflowed their Jacuzzi.

00:07:26.912 --> 00:07:28.313
[ Clears throat ]

00:07:28.313 --> 00:07:31.784
And then he proposes to her.
They can't get another room.

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:36.088
He proposes to her.
You -- You and your wife?

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:38.223
-Yeah. Well, no, my partner.

00:07:38.223 --> 00:07:39.691
-Girlfriend.
You and your partner.

00:07:39.691 --> 00:07:41.293
-Yeah.
-Are out of control, by the way.

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:43.629
Just two out-of-control idiots.

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:45.698
-We just have a different
perspective on life.

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:48.267
-Okay. I think it starts
with you riding a Jet Ski

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:49.468
and she's doing bong rips.

00:07:49.468 --> 00:07:50.769
-Yeah.
-Anyways...

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:52.838
That's how you meet
those people.

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:55.073
Anyways, they go, "Hey..."
-One guy. "Yeah!"

00:07:55.073 --> 00:07:57.676
-I know. He's like, "I've done
that! I've done that!"

00:07:57.676 --> 00:07:58.744
-"Yeah!"
-Yeah.

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:01.147
So then, you go,
"Hey, stay in our room.

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:02.848
You guys are in love.
You're lovebirds.

00:08:02.848 --> 00:08:05.017
Stay in our -- We don't even
have to see each other."

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:06.351
-Yeah.
-"Just stay in our..."

00:08:06.351 --> 00:08:07.887
And that's how
the movie kicks off,

00:08:07.887 --> 00:08:10.590
and then
just ridiculousness ensues.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:13.893
It is so funny.
Did I set it up correctly?

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:15.394
-What's that?
-Did I set it up correctly?

00:08:15.394 --> 00:08:17.429
-[Bleep]. I hope they watch it.
You gave them the whole movie.

00:08:17.429 --> 00:08:20.666
-Yeah, I know. Well, yeah.
Did I go too much?

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:23.102
Did I go too much? It's so good.
I want to show --

00:08:23.102 --> 00:08:25.737
Here's John Cena in
"Vacation Friends" on Hulu.

00:08:25.737 --> 00:08:27.906
Take a look.
-What's going on here?

00:08:27.906 --> 00:08:31.009
-Oh. Uh, we lost the brakes
around Marietta.

00:08:31.009 --> 00:08:33.278
E-brake did the yeoman's work
till right about now.

00:08:33.278 --> 00:08:35.781
Yo, chief! Just in case
you need to move it.

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:37.883
-Thank you!
-Ha!

00:08:37.883 --> 00:08:40.519
-So, I think -- I think
what Marcus is trying to ask

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:42.854
is, what are you two doing here?

00:08:42.854 --> 00:08:45.190
-Oh! Well, you guys,
we were so confused

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:46.925
why you didn't call
after Mexico.

00:08:46.925 --> 00:08:48.861
I mean, come on.
We were literally sitting

00:08:48.861 --> 00:08:50.963
by the phone for a week
being like, "What?"

00:08:50.963 --> 00:08:54.733
-But it was my bad, 'cause
the card I gave you -- old card.

00:08:54.733 --> 00:08:55.934
You had no way to call.

00:08:55.934 --> 00:08:57.403
-Yeah, so we did
a little Internet stalking,

00:08:57.403 --> 00:08:58.904
and then we found out
you guys were registered

00:08:58.904 --> 00:09:01.073
at Williams-Sonoma
in beautiful Atlanta.

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:03.609
-From there, it was easy.
Hit every wedding in Atlanta

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:04.777
starting with downtown,

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:06.445
working our way out
in concentric circles.

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:07.780
Classic circle-sweep maneuver.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.615
Same thing I used
to find lost kids in the cave.

00:09:09.615 --> 00:09:12.184
-This time,
you weren't too late, sweetie.

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:15.821
-That's what I'm talking about.
John Cena!

00:09:15.821 --> 00:09:18.624
"Vacation Friends"
is streaming now on Hulu.

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:20.859
John and I
are going head-to-head

00:09:20.859 --> 00:09:24.196
in a game of Facebreakers
when we come back. Stick around.

